## Context

Trial of 2026-09-25 from doudou (Playwright, headless, the author's cookies):
the blocked ADB project pages go through (200, correct title); aser.sn fails on
a certificate with the wrong domain name; the itie.sn PDF goes through under
Chromium (Firefox rejects an incomplete chain). Without cookies, ADB returns the
Cloudflare page. The remaining `fetch_error` rows are mostly certificates, not
robots.

The author decided: collection runs on padme; he clears the checks and logins
himself through a padme screen forwarded to doudou; sites with an invalid
certificate are collected and the error is recorded.

## Actions

1. "Driven browser" rung on padme: Playwright with a persistent profile specific
   to padme; display forwarded to doudou (X11 over SSH, waypipe or VNC: try and
   document) so the author can clear a check or log in. No cookie travels from
   doudou to padme.
2. The bytes kept are the **server response**, not the rendered page; the
   rendered page is kept only as a complement when it carries the information
   (tabs built by JavaScript).
3. Collection methods renamed and completed:
   `script`, `script-cookies` (formerly `browser-session`), `browser-automated`,
   `browser-manual`, `archive-record` (Web Archive and Common Crawl copies,
   currently counted as `script`), `local-record`. Schema, registries, site,
   tests, documentation.
4. Invalid certificate: collect, record the error in the row.
5. ADB pilot: the 7 agreements and 2 RRPs of projects 56140-001 and
   56368-001, and the PDF fact sheet of each project (56140-001, 56368-001,
   58342-001) become sources and are collected.
6. dgMarket: `sen-irve-framework-tender-2026` is deactivated (same notice as
   `sen-afd-irve-ami12-2026`, already collected). The attachments
   (`sen-irve-attachments-107072743`) require an account: if the author creates
   one, credentials go in `~/.config/keys/dgmarket.env`, read at login time
   only (`.claude/rules/keystore.md`).
7. Objects collected on padme are captured by DVC on padme.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The ADB pilot is collected on padme (`browser-automated`), bytes verified by fingerprint, titles re-read
- [ ] The certificate `fetch_error` rows are rerun; each row states the result and, where relevant, the certificate error
- [ ] No row still carries an old method value; the site shows the six labels
- [ ] Positive control of the forwarded screen: a Cloudflare check cleared by the author from doudou unblocks collection on padme
- [ ] No cookie, token or credential in a log, a commit or a ticket
- [ ] `make check-fast` and `make lint` green
